infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title DataLoader vs lookahead: one trip per level vs one JOIN
  desc Lookahead collapses nested trips into a single JOIN — by spending the per-field isolation DataLoader preserves
  compares
    - label DataLoader (batch per level)
      children
        - label Fixes "N queries, one column"
          desc Batches the sibling .load() calls at one resolver level into a single WHERE id IN (...) query
        - label Per-field isolation preserved
          desc Each resolver stays independent and knows nothing about its children
        - label 3 nested levels = 3 trips
          desc posts { author { profile { bio } } } buffers each level separately — three round-trips, not one
        - label Safe default everywhere
          desc The baseline batching every resolver should already have
    - label Lookahead (one JOIN)
      children
        - label Reads the info AST selection set
          desc The top-level resolver inspects which child fields the client actually requested
        - label Collapses nesting into 1 JOIN
          desc Three independent DataLoader trips become one joined SQL query
        - label Breaks per-field isolation
          desc The top resolver now changes behaviour based on which descendant fields were selected
        - label Last resort — measure first
          desc Use only when per-level DataLoader leaves observable latency
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b
